  "details": "Since last months, i noticed the unpleasant problem with VRChat.\n\nIf i stay for a while in the VRChat world with many people, a busy world, and i want jump to other world, i saw on more used W10 system very long unloading progress, makes my fps drops all the way down to 5 fps and everything froze almost (and frame drops on stream). This takes even minutes and unloading progress takes even more time in freeze part. It's so worst i am forced to restart VRChat.\n\nWith new install W11, i carefully observed unloading and notice again same fps drop to 5-10 fps, lucky much shorter for ~20-30 sec then it finally loads next world. The unloading problems are still there.\n\nThis points out there is something wrong with VRChat lately. I have almost no problems with world jumping some months ago, but now in last months the unloading times are really annoying and getting worser. \n\nBecause i have no problems for long time and i keep my system good maintained and clean, i have feeling VRChat does in last versions poor job in unloading worlds.\n\nIf i jump faster around even it's busy, unloading time is much shorter. If alone in the world, then also less problems. Only if i stay longer in the world with many people, then it's getting worse, even i am good in the world itself with decent fps, it's just weird to see why unloading progress is really bad.\n\nI want ask everyone to report the unloading problems. If you experience also same problems with unloading, please post here. I hope developers can look at it.\n\nMy system is RTX3060Ti, 32GB RAM and 5800X3D. That is still good system for VR.\n\nI have videos and streams as example, will link them later below.",
